[32m+[m[32m# DermaSense[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDermaSense is a monorepo containing a machine learning pipeline for skin image analysis, a FastAPI inference backend, and a Next.js frontend user interface.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Project Structure[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32m.[m
[32m+[m[32m├── backend/         # FastAPI application serving ML predictions[m
[32m+[m[32m├── frontend/        # Next.js 16 web application (React, Tailwind)[m
[32m+[m[32m├── ml/              # PyTorch training pipeline, notebooks, and models[m
[32m+[m[32m└── inspect_model.py # Model inspection utility[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Quick Start[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 1. Backend (FastAPI)[m
[32m+[m[32mThe backend exposes the inference API endpoints.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcd backend[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m venv .venv[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Activate the virtual environment:[m
[32m+[m[32m# Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate[m
[32m+[m[32m# macOS/Linux: source .venv/bin/activate[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpip install -r requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32muvicorn app.main:app --reload[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m*Note: Create an `.env` file in `backend/` if your configuration requires specific environment variables.*[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2. Frontend (Next.js)[m
[32m+[m[32mThe frontend provides the user-facing web application.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcd frontend[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm install[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m*Note: Set up an `.env.local` file in `frontend/` if environment variables are required (e.g., API endpoints).*[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 3. Machine Learning (PyTorch)[m
[32m+[m[32mThe `ml/` directory contains data processing scripts, PyTorch models, and Jupyter notebooks.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcd ml[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m venv .venv[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Activate the virtual environment:[m
[32m+[m[32m# Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate[m
[32m+[m[32m# macOS/Linux: source .venv/bin/activate[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpip install -r requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mTo explore the data or model training, launch Jupyter:[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mjupyter notebook[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
